  "_provenance": [
    "Float reference parameters for the procedural 16-wedge connectome (connectome.build_procedural).",
    "Tuned 2026-09-19 in a Claude Code session. The brief's starting point saturated every population: with syn_decay 0.8 one spike delivers ~5*w of charge against a threshold of 1.",
    "Path: random search, then evolutionary refinement (scratch tooling, not in the repo), found a slow-synapse regime with one persistent bump. T3 uses push-pull drive (+d PEN_L, -d PEN_R), per the user's decision: PEN_L-only drive above the PEN threshold current turns the bump clockwise (see tests.t3_phases).",
    "Retuned 2026-09-19 when the suite began checking T2 (with the bump set within 1 wedge of the landmark) and T3 from every start wedge (user decision): the previous values still passed at nominal but failed the +/-10% gate (5/10 one-at-a-time configs failed from 1-6 of the 16 headings). The user chose to retune rather than relax the gate. Search scored on robustness (scratch tooling): nominal, then one-at-a-time +/-10%, then +/-15%, 5 seeds, every start wedge, graded by the fraction of cases passing. Rounded to 4 significant figures, then verified with the real suite (T1-T8, including T7) and tune.py --robustness.",
    "Robustness: one-at-a-time +/-10% passes 10/10 on 5 seeds (the gate); +/-15% passes 3/10. All-at-once corners at +/-10% pass 11/32 (recorded, not gated). At nominal, a review session ran the suite on held-out seeds 5-24: all pass. The demo sequence (T3 after the 2000-tick hold) turns CCW and faster with drive on seeds 0-9.",
    "Units: 1 tick = dt ms; currents in the model's units, where the threshold current is v_thresh/tau."
